# AGENTS.md — noerd/{{module-name}}

Contributor notes for humans and AI agents working on the {{ModuleName}} module. The rules for
building WITH noerd (lists, details, pages, modals, modules, tests) come from the `noerd/noerd`
Boost guideline and skills; the module-specific rules are in
`resources/boost/guidelines/core.blade.php`. Both are rendered into the host project's agent files
by `php artisan boost:update` (add `noerd/{{module-name}}` to the `packages` array in `boost.json`).

## Layout

- `app-configs/{{module-name}}/` — YAML templates (lists/, details/, navigation.yml); the installed
  copy lives in the host's `app-configs/{{module-name}}/` — change both
- `resources/views/components/` — Livewire single-file components (`{{models}}-list.blade.php`,
  `{{model}}-detail.blade.php`), flat, Livewire namespace `{{module-name}}::`
- `src/Models/`, `src/Commands/`, `src/Providers/{{ModuleName}}ServiceProvider.php`
- `database/migrations|factories|seeders/`, `tests/` (Pest), `resources/lang/de.json`

## Commands

- `php artisan noerd:install-{{module-name}}` — first installation (asks for the tenant assignment)
- `php artisan noerd:update-{{module-name}}` — idempotent YAML update, discovered by `noerd:update-all`

## Working on the module

- Tests: `php artisan test --compact app-modules/{{module-name}}/tests` (Pest; tests prove
  mechanics, never the current YAML configuration)
- Format with the host project's `vendor/bin/pint --dirty` from the project root
- Keep the module independent of other optional modules; project-specific fields go into
  `custom_attributes`, never into module code or module YAML
- When a feature changes: update the YAML in both places, `resources/lang/de.json`, the tests and
  `resources/boost/guidelines/core.blade.php`
